From f24271f105d728d5de0f5f3b369a33d04db0ad1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:31:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(gpu): cut the stock onto a keyframe layer on the GPU
 (S3a)

The S2 kernel cut only from the empty floor, so a playback could not
continue from a keyframe on the GPU. Add the incremental start:

- cut.wgsl cs_encode turns a layer back into ordered keys in place;
- CutKernel::cut_into cuts into a caller buffer with no read-back (the
  viewport cut buffer, for S3c); CutKernel::run_onto reads it back;
- cut_cpu_onto is the CPU law (bit-exact to the one-batch cut);
- cut_onto_or_cpu(_on) takes the fallback rule of cut_or_cpu: the
  CAMCRAFT_GPU_COMPUTE=off switch, no adapter, a lost device, a kernel
  error or a failed spot check give the CPU law with the reason;
- a base layer with a wrong size or a non-finite value is refused.

cut_gpu.rs is split along the buffer seam into cut_buf.rs (400 lines).
Pinned by crates/gpu/tests/cut_onto.rs; it uses only the shared device
(#3589) and runs the switch and device-loss cases in a child process.

Refs #2629

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
